{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And let the earth bring forth a living soul</b> — a general statement for what fire and water and earth brought forth, also man." "<b>Behemah.</b> For they are with human beings for their needs, to ride and to eat." "<b>And creeping things.</b> They are the small creatures that go upon the earth." "<b>And the beast of the earth</b> — that it is blood in the field where there is no settlement, and the final vav is added in the word וחיתו, like למעינו מים (Psalms 114:5), בנו בעור (Numbers 24:3)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {3 "Reading שדם ('blood') as written; possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:39.424976329Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}